  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "Find, in ascending powers of $a,$ the **first three terms** in the binomial expansion of ${(1-2a)}^{9}.$\n\n$(1-2a)^{9}=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,+\\,\u22ef$",
  "worked_solution": "The first three terms of the binomial expansion for $(1+x)^{n}$ are given by\n\n$$\n(1+x)^{n}=1+nx+\\frac{n(n-1)}{2!}{x}^{2}+\u22ef.\n$$\n\nBy substituting $x=-2a$ and $n=9$ into the above formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(1-2a)}^{9} & =1+9\\cdot (-2a)+\\frac{9(9-1)}{2!}\\cdot (-2a)^{2}+\u22ef \\\\  & =1-18a+\\frac{9\\cdot 8}{2}\\cdot 4{a}^{2}+\u22ef \\\\  & =1-18a+36\\cdot 4{a}^{2}+\u22ef \\\\  & =1-18a+144{a}^{2}+\u22ef\\end{aligned}\n$$",
